Not if you mean "kill" when you say "handle".

A water demon is as fast as you, provided you're unburdened.  If you
manage to get a distance between the two of you, you can just run
away.  This means exploring the level fully, having a clear escape
route to both stairs, and leaving a distraction (like a weapon or a
piece of armor or a strategic engraving).

Water mocassins are a different issue.  They also respect Elbereth, so
you can try to escape into a corridor and finish them off one by one,
but you have to take a step away from the fountain in order to
engrave.  This means you need an additional turn before you can catch
a breath, and this may well kill you.

